B 0x95EB THE ACCELERATION TOWARDS THE SHIP COMES FROM A TABLE OF 256 WORDS
B 0x95EB For an object to curve towards the ship it needs a vertical and a
B 0x95EB horizontal acceleration, and here they are not calculated: they are looked
B 0x95EB up. The two differences are taken in absolute value, the high nibble of
B 0x95EB one is joined with the high nibble of the other in a single byte, and that
B 0x95EB byte (times two) indexes the table at 0x9657, which is 256 words. It is
B 0x95EB read twice, crossing the nibbles, and that gives the two components; the
B 0x95EB sign is set by the two's complement.
