F 0x9BD2 16
B 0x9BFB THE OPTION'S QUEUE IS FILLED USING THE STACK
B 0x9BFB The options follow the ship with a delay: its last sixteen positions
B 0x9BFB have to be kept. When they are created, that queue is filled in one go
B 0x9BFB with the current position, and to do that the cartridge does something
B 0x9BFB you do not see every day: it points the STACK POINTER at the queue
B 0x9BFB (`ld sp,hl`), does eight `push bc` in a row (sixteen bytes in sixteen
B 0x9BFB instructions) and restores SP, all with interrupts disabled so that
B 0x9BFB nobody uses the stack in the meantime.
L 0x9BFB set_up_one_option   Copies the ship's position into the option's card and fills its position queue with `push`
C 0x9BFB 0xE20B: how many options there are
C 0x9BFF With one, the position comes from the ship; with two, from the first option
C 0x9C10 The X and the Y
C 0x9C11 The X and the Y
C 0x9C12 The Y
C 0x9C23 Pattern 0x44 and colour 0x0A
C 0x9C25 Pattern 0x44
C 0x9C2F The stack pointer is saved...
C 0x9C36 ...pointed at the queue...
C 0x9C39 ...eight `push`: sixteen bytes in one go...
C 0x9C3D ...and restored
L 0x9C41 run_options   Every two frames pushes the ship's position into the queue, and the options come out at the other end
C 0x9C41 Not with the screen stopped
C 0x9C4B Nor without options
C 0x9C4E Not without options
C 0x9C57 With the joystick still or on an exact diagonal, the queue does not advance
C 0x9C5A The four direction bits
C 0x9C5C With the joystick still, the queue does not advance
C 0x9C66 With two options, both
C 0x9C67 Nor on an exact diagonal
L 0x9C74 shift_one_queue   Pushes the new position in at the front and shifts the sixteen bytes of the queue
C 0x9C7A The new position, at the front
C 0x9C81 Fourteen bytes: the rest of the queue
C 0x9C86 And the one from sixteen frames ago, at the end
C 0x9C87 0x3C bytes back
L 0x9C90 animate_options   Every two frames advances the options' drawing, four round and round, from the table at 0x9CBA
C 0x9C91 0xE182: one in every two frames
C 0x9C9C 0xE183: which drawing they are on
C 0x9C9D With two options, both
C 0x9CAF Four drawings round and round
D 0x9CBA 0x9CC2 option_drawings  Four (pattern, colour) pairs the option blinks with. Read by 0x9CA9.
F 0x9CBA 2
L 0x9CC2 release_fire_button   0xE180 to zero: the button has been released
L 0x9CC5 check_fire   With the button just pressed, or held for fifteen frames, the ship and its two options fire
C 0x9CC5 Not with the screen stopped
C 0x9CCA Nor with the ship dead
C 0x9CD2 Bit 4 of what was just pressed: fire
C 0x9CD9 And bit 4 of the joystick: held
